<title>FRANCE: EU cuts daily refund on soft wheat flour exports.</title>
<headline>EU cuts daily refund on soft wheat flour exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday cut the daily refund on exports of soft wheat flour to 22 Ecus per tonne from a previous level of 27 Ecus, grain traders said.</p>
<p>Industry sources linked the move to a decrease in the amount of the rebate the EU granted for wheat grain exports.</p>
<p>At its weekly grain auction the EU lowered the rebate on wheat grain exports to 15.97 Ecus from last week's level of 22.35 Ecus.</p>
<p>The flour rebate is usually linked to the wheat rebate. To reach a flour rebate the wheat figure is usually multipled by a coefficient of 1.37.  </p>
<p>The move is likely to disappoint European millers, who had been pressing for a higher flour refund this week.</p>
<p>Last week the EU kept the rebate for wheat flour exports unchanged at 27 Ecus per tonne, although it raised the rebate applying to wheat grain exports.</p>
<p>But world wheat prices have firmed, easing pressure for higher EU wheat subsidies.</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
